"""Little Round Top: Gettysburg, 2 July 1863.  A sample game for the
Grognard engine.

The second day.  Longstreet's attack on the Union left begins with
Hood's division, sent east across the farms below Warfield Ridge toward
two rocky hills, the Round Tops, and the boulders of Devil's Den.  The
smaller hill, which looks down the whole Union line, has no one on it
but a few signal officers.  Play either side against the computer, or
against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./roundtop (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.roundtop.json.  ./roundtop --selftest checks the map and
plays a game between two computer players.
"""

